can be switched off by introducing conditions that stabilize B-DNA, while it can be fueled by adding Z-DNA-promoting high-saline buffer. When MgCl_{2} was used as external stimulus, 70% of the motors rotated, while 76% of the stators/controls exhibited no rotation. Such a motor system could be successfully applied to perform multiple actions aimed for our benefit. Moreover, for the first time we have directly observed the B–Z conformational transition of DNA in real-time, which shed light on the fundamental understanding of DNA conformations.\n\nSubjects Salts, Conformation, Genetics, Nucleic acid structure, DNA origami\n\n## Supporting Information\n\nAdditional information as noted in text. This material is available free of charge via the Internet at http://pubs.acs.org.\n\n\nsifile1- pdf file\n\nsifile2- avi file\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nDirect and Real-Time Observation of Rotary Movement of a DNA Nanomechanical Device (https://openalex.org/W2018036217)\nciteturn55search3 [wordlim: 200] Published: 13.9 years ago; Crawled: 2 months ago; DOI: 10.1021/ja310454k\n# Direct and Real-Time Observation of Rotary Movement of a DNA Nanomechanical Device\n\nOpenAlex ID: W2018036217\n\nDOI: 10.1021/ja310454k\n\nPMID: 23311576\n\nType: article\n\nYear: 2012\n\nPublication date: 2012-12-19\n\nLanguage: en\n\n## Source\n\nName: Journal of the American Chemical Society\n\nISSN-L: 0002-7863\n\nISSN: 0002-7863, 1520-5126, 1943-2984\n\nPublisher: American Chemical Society\n\n## Citation\n\nVolume: 135\n\nIssue: 3\n\nPages: 1117–1123\n\n## Article links\n\n  * Article website\n  * Location website\n\n## Authors\n\n  * Arivazhagan Rajendran (ORCID) — Kyoto University (ROR)\n  * Masayuki Endo (ORCID) — Kyoto University (ROR); Japan Science and Technology Agency (ROR)\n  * Kumi Hidaka — Kyoto University (ROR)\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nVolume 135 Issue 3 | Journal of the 